    {
      "id": "C1",
      "priority": "P1",
      "path": "tooling/xtask/src/tasks/android_reference_membership.rs",
      "line": 1013,
      "title": "Split traversal mutates a module borrowed through attribute()",
      "finding": "The Option<&Literal> returned by attribute(module, \"split_test_targets\") borrows the whole ModuleFact. The borrowed dictionary entries are consumed across the loop. In the non-dictionary configuration branch, module.unresolved.push requires a mutable borrow while the immutable whole-module borrow is still live for later iterations. This is a source-inferred E0502 build blocker; no compiler was run.",
      "requested_change": "Accumulate split validation issues independently and append them after borrowed entry traversal, or establish disjoint field borrows explicitly. Retain the invalid-configuration evidence and every existing assertion.",
      "acceptance": "Normal locked xtask compilation under a granted runtime lease; a meaningful non-dictionary split configuration regression remains explicitly unresolved rather than producing trusted split membership."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "priority": "P2",
      "path": "tooling/xtask/src/tasks/android_reference_membership.rs",
      "line": 1018,
      "title": "Explicit null split tags are incorrectly treated as automatic membership",
      "finding": "strings() maps Literal::None to an empty vector. For split_test_targets = {\"a\": {\"tags\": None, \"test_filter\": \"com.sample\"}}, derive_relationships consequently emits split a with aggregate_membership = true. The pinned producer uses list(split_target.get(\"tags\", default = [])); the default applies only to an absent key, and an explicitly null value cannot be converted to the producer list. The source relationship therefore overstates this invalid configuration. Similar explicitly invalid inner data/additional_jvm_args values must not be treated as accepted producer inputs.",
      "reference": "tooling/xtask/test_data/reference_membership/sources/base/bazel/bazel.bzl:1019 (tags conversion), 1057 (split data), 1021 (additional_jvm_args conversion)",
      "requested_change": "Validate the supported per-split producer input shapes, distinguishing missing keys from explicit null. Retain raw literal attributes and explicit unresolved reasons; suppress trusted child/aggregate membership for invalid or unsupported configuration instead of interpreting null as an empty list.",
      "acceptance": "Add non-weakening regressions for explicit tags=None plus representative invalid per-split data/additional_jvm_args and non-dictionary configurations. Keep source-derived membership conditional and runtime counts null."
    }
  ],
